hey this is presh talwalkar  on a table are nine face up cards  each card displays a different number  from the list  two four eight sixteen thirty two sixty  four one twenty eight two fifty six and  five hundred twelve  alice and bob play a game where they  alternately take turns  each picks a single card on a turn and  alice goes first  once a card is chosen it cannot be  selected again  the game ends when someone wins or all  the cards have been selected  the winner is the first person to  collect a set of three cards with a  product of thirty two thousand seven  hundred and sixty eight  for example in the game just illustrated  alice collects the cards 416 and 512  which have a product of 32 768 so alice  wins that game  but there could be other games in which  bob selects a set of three cards that  have a product of 32  768.  in that case bob would be the winner  but there could also be games in which  alice gets a set of cards and bob gets a  set of cards but neither have collected  a set in which there are three cards  that have a product of 32  768.  in that case the game ends in a draw  the problem is if both play optimally  does either player have a winning  strategy  or does the game always end in a draw  and how should you play this game  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for the  solution  the game seems like it's impossible to  solve  how can you keep track of all the  possible ways that they can pick numbers  and how can a person know if a set of  three numbers even has a product of  32768  amazingly the game has a simple solution  and you probably already know how to  solve it  if you've been watching my videos long  enough you already might know the trick  so we'll start out with the simple game  of tic-tac-toe  imagine that alice plays x on this three  by three grid and bob plays o  they take turns hoping to be the first  to make three in a row  now as you  know if both play optimally each can  block the other perfectly so that  neither player can make three in a row  resulting in a draw game  now let's consider a new game  we'll first write the numbers 1 through  9 in the grid to make a magic square  we'll have each row column and diagonal  have a sum of 15.  that is this row this row and this row  each row has a sum of 15.  each column has a sum of 15  and each diagonal has a sum of 15.  furthermore this arrangement is unique  up to rotation and reflection so there's  no other three by three magic square  with the numbers one through nine and  the only triplets with the sum of 15 are  in the rows columns and diagonals  so now consider a game alice and bob  takes turns selecting cards and the  first person to have three cards with  the sum of 15 wins  let's mark alice's cards with an x and  bob's cards with an  o now after the second move bob has to  block alice's three in a row by picking  nine  now alice has to block the three in a  row by picking one  bob plays somewhere and then alice has  to block three in a row by picking three  then bob has to block  and then the game ends in a draw  as you can see the strategy to this game  is just like tic-tac-toe  if played optimally by both the game is  sure to end in a draw you simply pick  numbers  in which you would pick the same spot in  tic-tac-toe  so how does this relate to the race to  32  768  what we'll do is we'll do a  transformation to each number  for each number x in this magic square  we'll replace it with the new number 2  to the power of x so the number 4  becomes 2 to the power of 4 which is 16.  9 becomes 2 to the power of 9 which is  512.  we'll replace each entry in this magic  square with 2 to the power of that entry  what we have now is a multiplicative  magic square  each row column and diagonal has the  product equal to 2 to the power of 15  which is 32  768.  so now we analyze the race to 32  768.  if we mark alice's choices as x's  and bob's choices as os then the game  has the same strategy as tic-tac-toe  after a few moves we know where alice  has to go to block bob from making three  numbers who have a product of 32 768.  furthermore bob knows where he has to  pick in order to block alice's three in  a row  so if both play optimally the game is  just like tic tac toe and it should end  in a draw  not only should it end in a draw but  there is a simple way that each player  can select cards to block the other  player  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on facebook google plus and  patreon you can catch me on social media  at preshtalwalker and if you like this  video please check out my books there  are links in the video description

